>give violin to demon
"Wondrous fine, master! But one treasure is yet to be given!"

>give key to demon
"This will do for my fee. 'Tis a paltry hoard, but as you have done me a small
service by loosing me from this wizard, it will suffice."

>demon, give me the wand
"I hear and obey!" says the demon. He stretches out an enormous hand towards the
wand. The Wizard is unsure what to do, pointing it threateningly at the demon,
then at you. "Fudge!" he cries, but aside from a strong odor of chocolate in the
air, there is no effect. The demon plucks the wand out of his hand (it's about
toothpick-size to him) and gingerly lays it before you. He fades into the smoke,
which disperses. The wizard runs from the room in terror.

>take wand
Taken.

